Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.56,0:00:25.70,Title,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}《福尔摩斯历险记》
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.48,0:01:14.40,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}巴克利夫人 您的茶\N{\fnArial\fs30}Mrs. Barclay, your tea.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.49,0:01:17.70,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}这么多年了 你怎么做得出这种事？\N{\fnArial\fs30}All these years, how could you do such a thing?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.82,0:01:19.53,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}您的茶 夫人\N{\fnArial\fs30}Your tea, madam.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.62,0:01:21.08,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}哦 我恨你 我恨你\N{\fnArial\fs30}Oh, I hate you, I hate you, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.20,0:01:23.50,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我恨你 恨死你了\N{\fnArial\fs30}I hate you, I hate you.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.58,0:01:24.54,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}大卫…\N{\fnArial\fs30}David…{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.62,0:01:26.12,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}您的茶 夫人\N{\fnArial\fs30}Your tea, madam.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.25,0:01:27.67,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}大卫 你背叛了他\N{\fnArial\fs30}David, you betrayed him.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.75,0:01:29.00,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}范尼夫人…\N{\fnArial\fs30}Mrs. Fenning…{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.08,0:01:33.13,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}发生了什么事 怎么啦 孩子？\N{\fnArial\fs30}What's happened, what is it, child?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.26,0:01:34.59,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是夫人和上校\N{\fnArial\fs30}It's madam and the Colonel, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.72,0:01:36.22,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}里面吵得吓人\N{\fnArial\fs30}something awful is going on{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.30,0:01:37.76,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我打不开门\N{\fnArial\fs30}and I can't open the door.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.84,0:01:39.89,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}让开 我来试试\N{\fnArial\fs30}Here, let me try.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.60,0:01:44.81,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}快阻止他 你们两个\N{\fnArial\fs30}Stop him, both of you.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.93,0:01:46.48,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}巴克利夫人\N{\fnArial\fs30}Mrs. Barclay, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.60,0:01:48.98,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}巴克利夫人 快开门\N{\fnArial\fs30}Mrs. Barclay, open the door.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.30,0:02:16.97,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}巴克利夫人 快开门啊\N{\fnArial\fs30}Mrs. Barclay, open the door.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.09,0:02:18.26,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}门从里面反锁了\N{\fnArial\fs30}The door is locked on the inside as well, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.38,0:02:20.76,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}没有钥匙\N{\fnArial\fs30}and there's no key.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.84,0:02:24.06,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我去找医生 还有警察\N{\fnArial\fs30}I'm going out for a doctor, and the police.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.95,0:02:37.81,Title,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}《驼背人》
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.38,0:03:02.01,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他们人还不少\N{\fnArial\fs30}There's quite a few of them{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.14,0:03:04.14,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我受伤回家之前是\N{\fnArial\fs30}when I sailed home wounded.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.22,0:03:06.81,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他在印度功勋卓著\N{\fnArial\fs30}Had a good record out in India, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.89,0:03:08.68,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}尤其平叛那两次 大获全胜\N{\fnArial\fs30}did wonders during the Mutiny.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.81,0:03:11.10,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你接手这个案子 肯定不会后悔的\N{\fnArial\fs30}I'm sure you won't regret taking the case.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.19,0:03:13.52,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}啊 哨兵\N{\fnArial\fs30}Ah, sentry.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.20,0:03:27.95,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}约翰·华生医生 前陆军军医\N{\fnArial\fs30}Dr. John Watson, formerly medical officer{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.04,0:03:30.04,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}隶属波克夏步兵团\N{\fnArial\fs30}attached to the Royal Berkshires, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.12,0:03:31.50,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}现在是私人医师\N{\fnArial\fs30}now in civilian practice.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.58,0:03:33.08,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}墨斐 副将\N{\fnArial\fs30}Murphy, second in command, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.21,0:03:35.79,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}暂时接管麦洛斯步兵团\N{\fnArial\fs30}temporarily in charge of the Royal Mallows, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.88,0:03:38.17,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}由于我们上校惨死一事\N{\fnArial\fs30}following the, tragedy of our Colonel's death.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.26,0:03:40.26,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}这位一定是福尔摩斯先生？\N{\fnArial\fs30}And this will be Mr. Holmes?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.38,0:03:41.84,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}请进\N{\fnArial\fs30}Please.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.72,0:03:50.27,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}您能及时赶到真是太好了\N{\fnArial\fs30}It's good of you to come so swiftly.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.39,0:03:51.94,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}别客气\N{\fnArial\fs30}Not at all.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.06,0:03:54.52,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我向福尔摩斯解释了您一定\N{\fnArial\fs30}I have explained to Holmes how concerned{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.61,0:03:58.07,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}为可能形成的丑闻十分忧虑\N{\fnArial\fs30}you must be about the possibility of a scandal.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.15,0:04:01.90,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}多谢\N{\fnArial\fs30}Thank you.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.03,0:04:06.37,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我很担心我们团的荣誉\N{\fnArial\fs30}The honor of the regiment is in my care.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.45,0:04:09.83,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但是 报纸上的报道暗示\N{\fnArial\fs30}And yet, the newspapers report suggest{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.91,0:04:12.54,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}丑闻是不可避免的\N{\fnArial\fs30}that a scandal is inevitable.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.66,0:04:14.00,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}当然不会\N{\fnArial\fs30}Surely not.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.08,0:04:15.92,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我已经竭尽全力将记者\N{\fnArial\fs30}I've done my utmost to make sure that reporters{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.04,0:04:17.79,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}挡在事态之外\N{\fnArial\fs30}were kept as far away as possible.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.92,0:04:20.05,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}当然 这样会让他们更加怀疑\N{\fnArial\fs30}Exactly, and that is what has made them suspicious.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.17,0:04:22.59,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他们嗅到了秘密 这会让他们的\N{\fnArial\fs30}They scent a mystery, that much is clear{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.67,0:04:26.14,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}轻描淡写变成大做文章\N{\fnArial\fs30}from the little they have been able to say.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.26,0:04:30.72,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}当然 不应该反反复复\N{\fnArial\fs30}Surely, it would be wrong to repeat, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.81,0:04:33.56,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}招惹他们注意…\N{\fnArial\fs30}to draw attention to…{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.64,0:04:37.56,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}的确\N{\fnArial\fs30}Quite.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.65,0:04:47.20,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我们非常需要您的帮助 福尔摩斯先生\N{\fnArial\fs30}You see how much we need your help, Mr. Holmes.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.28,0:04:51.04,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你觉得如何 福尔摩斯？\N{\fnArial\fs30}What do you say, Holmes?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.12,0:04:54.12,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}还能如何？\N{\fnArial\fs30}What can I say?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.25,0:04:57.88,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}墨斐少校 您说的都是废话\N{\fnArial\fs30}Major Murphy, you have told me nothing.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.96,0:04:59.38,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我来奥尔德肖特\N{\fnArial\fs30}I have come down here{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.46,0:05:02.17,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是受我的朋友劝说\N{\fnArial\fs30}after persuasion from my friend, to Aldershot, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.30,0:05:05.43,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他比我要更热心军队的事\N{\fnArial\fs30}who has more interest in military matters than I.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.51,0:05:17.44,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}现在我来了 就请告诉我实情\N{\fnArial\fs30}Now that I am here, please tell me the facts.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.52,0:05:19.69,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}本团司令官\N{\fnArial\fs30}The commanding officer of this regiment, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.82,0:05:21.15,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}詹姆斯·巴克利上校\N{\fnArial\fs30}Colonel James Barclay, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.23,0:05:22.94,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}被发现死在家中\N{\fnArial\fs30}was found dead in his villa{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.03,0:05:25.78,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}就在前天夜里10点\N{\fnArial\fs30}at about 10 o'clock the night before last.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.86,0:05:28.24,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}发现尸体的是列兵贝茨\N{\fnArial\fs30}The body was found by Private Bates, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.32,0:05:30.78,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他的勤务兵 尸体躺在起居室里\N{\fnArial\fs30}his batman, lying in the morning room.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.87,0:05:33.16,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}有一条两寸长的不规则伤口\N{\fnArial\fs30}There was a ragged cut, two-inches long, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.29,0:05:34.79,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}嵌在他脑后\N{\fnArial\fs30}on the back of his head, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.91,0:05:37.08,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}显然是被猛击造成的\N{\fnArial\fs30}which had evidently been caused by a violent blow{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.17,0:05:38.71,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}凶器是钝器\N{\fnArial\fs30}from a blunt instrument.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.83,0:05:40.67,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}尸体旁的地板上\N{\fnArial\fs30}And upon the floor by the body{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.79,0:05:47.68,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}有根手工制作的木质棍子\N{\fnArial\fs30}was a singular hand-carved wooden club.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.76,0:05:50.30,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}还有 沙发上躺着\N{\fnArial\fs30}Also, stretched out on the sofa{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.43,0:05:52.97,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}晕厥过去的南希·巴…\N{\fnArial\fs30}lying in a dead faint, was Nancy Bar…{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.06,0:05:55.81,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}巴克利夫人\N{\fnArial\fs30}Mrs. Barclay.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.93,0:06:01.65,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}请继续 墨斐少校\N{\fnArial\fs30}Please continue, Major Murphy.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.77,0:06:03.73,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}仆人留意到这场悲剧\N{\fnArial\fs30}The servants had been alerted to the tragedy{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.86,0:06:05.40,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是因为巴克利上校夫妇\N{\fnArial\fs30}by the sounds of a quarrel{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.53,0:06:07.65,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}发生了激烈争吵\N{\fnArial\fs30}between the Colonel and Mrs. Barclay.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.74,0:06:09.57,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他们试着闯进起居室\N{\fnArial\fs30}They tried to enter the morning room{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.70,0:06:11.16,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}却发现门锁上了\N{\fnArial\fs30}but found it locked.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.28,0:06:13.04,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}贝茨不得不绕到花园里\N{\fnArial\fs30}Bates had to go around by the garden{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.16,0:06:14.70,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}从落地窗进去\N{\fnArial\fs30}and get in through the french windows.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.83,0:06:16.62,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}而现在您怀疑是巴克利夫人干的？\N{\fnArial\fs30}And now you suspect Mrs. Barclay?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.71,0:06:17.83,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是的\N{\fnArial\fs30}Yes.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.96,0:06:19.50,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但她没能力\N{\fnArial\fs30}But she is quite incapable{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.63,0:06:23.21,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}做出如此可怕的举动\N{\fnArial\fs30}of such a dreadful act.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.34,0:06:25.01,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我做已故上校\N{\fnArial\fs30}I have been the late Colonel's{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.09,0:06:26.97,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}的副将很多年了\N{\fnArial\fs30}second in command for a number of years.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.05,0:06:32.01,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我了解南希·巴克利\N{\fnArial\fs30}I've come to know Nancy Barclay well.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.14,0:06:37.31,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}当然\N{\fnArial\fs30}Of course.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.39,0:06:39.69,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}跟我说说巴克利上校\N{\fnArial\fs30}Tell me about Colonel Barclay, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.77,0:06:43.48,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他是否受到手下士兵们的敬重？\N{\fnArial\fs30}was he highly regarded by the men under his command?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.57,0:06:46.99,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}考虑到他的背景 算很敬重了\N{\fnArial\fs30}Considering his background, remarkably so.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.07,0:06:50.03,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他的背景 怎么 他有不光彩的过去？\N{\fnArial\fs30}His background, why, was he ever disgraced?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.11,0:06:52.95,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}不 但外界通常不知道\N{\fnArial\fs30}No, but it's not generally known outside{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.08,0:06:55.91,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}吉姆·巴克利的军旅生涯\N{\fnArial\fs30}that Jim Barclay began his career{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.99,0:06:58.83,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}始于麦洛斯团普通列兵\N{\fnArial\fs30}as a private soldier in the Mallows.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.91,0:07:01.00,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}这是真的？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Did he, indeed?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.08,0:07:02.79,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}从列兵晋升到司令官\N{\fnArial\fs30}From private soldier to commanding officer{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.92,0:07:04.38,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}在同一个团里\N{\fnArial\fs30}in the same regiment, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.50,0:07:06.88,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}这可是罕见的成就\N{\fnArial\fs30}that's a rare achievement.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.96,0:07:08.38,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是他在印度叛乱中展现的勇气\N{\fnArial\fs30}I was his gallantry in the Indian Mutiny{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.47,0:07:10.51,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}让他赢得了这个职位\N{\fnArial\fs30}that got him his commission, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.59,0:07:15.60,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}之后的几年他连升三级\N{\fnArial\fs30}and then quite rapid promotion over the years, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.72,0:07:19.43,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我得说 比我快得多\N{\fnArial\fs30}more rapid than mine, for instance.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.56,0:07:22.73,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}令人印象深刻\N{\fnArial\fs30}Impressive.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.81,0:07:25.94,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我猜不幸的巴克利夫人被拘留了吧？\N{\fnArial\fs30}And I suppose the unfortunate Mrs. Barclay is in custody?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.07,0:07:30.07,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}不 不完全是 不是的\N{\fnArial\fs30}No, not exactly, no.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.20,0:07:32.61,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}她在住院 被严密看管\N{\fnArial\fs30}She's in hospital, being looked after, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.74,0:07:34.78,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}警官就站在床边\N{\fnArial\fs30}with a police constable standing by.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.29,0:07:41.12,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}南希·巴克利现在是个大方的女人\N{\fnArial\fs30}Nancy Barclay is a handsome woman now, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.25,0:07:42.71,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但你应该看看她\N{\fnArial\fs30}but you should have seen her{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.79,0:07:49.42,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}年轻时在印度 30年前的样子\N{\fnArial\fs30}as a young girl in India, 30 years ago.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.51,0:07:52.30,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}她是军团的女儿\N{\fnArial\fs30}She was a daughter of the regiment.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.43,0:07:56.89,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}她父亲是团部的军士长 RSM·迪威艾\N{\fnArial\fs30}Her father was the Regimental Sergeant Major, RSM Devoy, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.97,0:08:03.10,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}这么个岳父足以吓倒任何士兵\N{\fnArial\fs30}and therefore quite a formidable father-in-law for any soldier.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.23,0:08:05.27,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我记得我们一个连的弟兄\N{\fnArial\fs30}I remember that all the men in my company{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.40,0:08:09.61,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}都认为她是驻军里最漂亮的女孩\N{\fnArial\fs30}thought her quite the prettiest girl in the garrison.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.69,0:08:11.90,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}还是尉官的我 跟她接触不多\N{\fnArial\fs30}As a junior officer I had little to do with her, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.99,0:08:15.12,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但我清楚她是最有魅力\N{\fnArial\fs30}but I was aware that she was a most charming, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.24,0:08:19.66,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}最活泼而勇敢的女孩\N{\fnArial\fs30}most vivacious and spirited girl.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.88,0:08:29.13,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}理所当然\N{\fnArial\fs30}It was quite understandable{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.25,0:08:31.67,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}巴克利并非团里唯一一个想\N{\fnArial\fs30}that Barclay was not the only man in the regiment{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.80,0:08:34.30,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}执子之手的人\N{\fnArial\fs30}who sought her hand.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.43,0:08:38.14,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但最终 她选择了他\N{\fnArial\fs30}But, in the end, he was the one she chose.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.56,0:08:47.31,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他们在伯第结的婚 1858年的夏天\N{\fnArial\fs30}They were married at Bhurtee, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.44,0:08:49.78,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}离科尔普不远 之前几个月\N{\fnArial\fs30}not far from Cornpor a few months after{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.86,0:08:51.65,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}那块被围攻的驻军地\N{\fnArial\fs30}the besieged garrison there{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.74,0:08:53.82,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}刚被被尼尔将军的纵队解救\N{\fnArial\fs30}was relieved by General Neill's column{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.95,0:08:56.16,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}时值1858年夏天\N{\fnArial\fs30}in the summer of 1858.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.24,0:08:58.70,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}婚后不久\N{\fnArial\fs30}Shortly after the marriage, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.78,0:09:03.25,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}巴克利中士不出所料 受到了委任\N{\fnArial\fs30}Sergeant Barclay got his commission, as expected.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.37,0:09:04.83,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}巴克利一家\N{\fnArial\fs30}It must have been difficult{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.92,0:09:06.88,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}起先一定很受危难\N{\fnArial\fs30}for the Barclays at first, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.00,0:09:09.21,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}一个军士 在行伍中被晋升\N{\fnArial\fs30}NCO, promoted from the ranks, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.34,0:09:12.21,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}作为军士长的女婿？\N{\fnArial\fs30}married to a regimental Sergeant Major's daughter?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.30,0:09:18.01,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是的 我相信的确有些社会摩擦\N{\fnArial\fs30}Yes, I believe there was some little social friction.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.10,0:09:23.27,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但是 南希以高贵和魅力忍耐\N{\fnArial\fs30}But, Nancy carried it off with dignity and charm, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.39,0:09:26.31,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他们很快就被大家接受了\N{\fnArial\fs30}and they gained acceptance in no time.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.40,0:09:28.65,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}巴克利的事业蒸蒸日上\N{\fnArial\fs30}Barclay's career flourished, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.73,0:09:33.07,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}部队5年前撤出印度\N{\fnArial\fs30}and the regiment returned from India some five years ago.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.19,0:09:37.36,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}之后巴克利被委任为司令官\N{\fnArial\fs30}Barclay was then appointed to commanding officer.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.45,0:09:41.54,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他们的婚姻生活仍旧很幸福？\N{\fnArial\fs30}And the marriage continued to be a happy one?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.62,0:09:44.87,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}看起来是那样\N{\fnArial\fs30}It appeared to be so.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.00,0:09:46.25,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}看起来？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Appeared?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.37,0:09:48.04,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}大多数人相信他们的婚姻\N{\fnArial\fs30}Most people believe the marriage{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.13,0:09:52.71,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}一直是幸福美满的\N{\fnArial\fs30}to have been a uniformly happy one.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.84,0:09:57.26,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}那您认为呢 墨斐少校？\N{\fnArial\fs30}And what do you believe, Major Murphy?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.38,0:09:59.85,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}作为副将的我\N{\fnArial\fs30}My position as second in command{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.93,0:10:02.64,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}经常因公拜访巴克利夫妇\N{\fnArial\fs30}often took me to the Barclay's house.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.76,0:10:07.27,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我看到他们婚姻的另一面\N{\fnArial\fs30}I saw a different side to the marriage.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.39,0:10:10.23,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}真相的重要性\N{\fnArial\fs30}The truth is more important{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.31,0:10:14.65,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}远超过您对前任长官的忠诚\N{\fnArial\fs30}than loyalty to your late commander.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.78,0:10:17.86,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}有一晚 我在巴克利夫妇家中用餐\N{\fnArial\fs30}One night I had been dining at the Barclays.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.95,0:10:20.16,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}出门走到车道尽头\N{\fnArial\fs30}It wasn't until I reached the end of the drive{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.28,0:10:22.33,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}才发觉自己把雪茄盒\N{\fnArial\fs30}that I realized I'd left my cigar case{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.45,0:10:24.20,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}落在餐室里了\N{\fnArial\fs30}in the dining room.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.29,0:10:27.75,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我回去的时候 大门还是敞开的\N{\fnArial\fs30}I went back, the front door was still open;{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.83,0:10:30.08,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}简 那个女仆 在门厅里\N{\fnArial\fs30}Jane, the maid, was in the hall.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.13,0:10:33.38,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}真庆幸你还在这儿\N{\fnArial\fs30}I'm glad you're still here, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.46,0:10:35.09,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我把雪茄盒落在桌子上了\N{\fnArial\fs30}I left my cigar case on the table.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.21,0:10:36.76,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我想巴克利上校夫妇\N{\fnArial\fs30}I think the Colonel and Mrs. Barclay{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.84,0:10:38.59,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}已经就寝了 先生\N{\fnArial\fs30}have gone to bed, sir.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.72,0:10:40.59,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}哦 看在上帝的份上 简\N{\fnArial\fs30}Oh, for goodness sake, James.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.68,0:10:42.55,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}坦白吧 是谁 谁？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Confess then, who is it, who?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.64,0:10:47.23,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}放开我 你弄疼我了\N{\fnArial\fs30}Let go of me, you're hurting me.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.31,0:10:49.10,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}那就告诉我你爱我\N{\fnArial\fs30}Tell me you love me then, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.19,0:10:50.69,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}只爱我一个人\N{\fnArial\fs30}me and nobody else.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.81,0:10:52.44,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}听到我说的吗 听到没有？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Do you hear, do you hear me?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.56,0:10:55.57,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}哦 如果不爱你我又为什么嫁给你？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Oh, would I have married you if I didn't?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.65,0:10:59.07,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我不知道 有时候我也想不通\N{\fnArial\fs30}I don't know, sometimes I wonder.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.66,0:11:08.16,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}这些猜忌的表现\N{\fnArial\fs30}And this expression of jealousy{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.25,0:11:10.92,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}墨斐少校 就在您离开他们家\N{\fnArial\fs30}occurred within seconds of you, Major Murphy, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.00,0:11:12.75,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}几秒内爆发\N{\fnArial\fs30}leaving the Barclays' house.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.84,0:11:14.84,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}告诉我关于上校的事\N{\fnArial\fs30}Tell me about the Colonel, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.96,0:11:18.34,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他是否是个暴力的人？\N{\fnArial\fs30}was he a violent man in any way?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.47,0:11:20.51,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}偶尔为之\N{\fnArial\fs30}On occasion.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.63,0:11:22.14,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他会十分残暴地\N{\fnArial\fs30}He could be most vindictive{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.22,0:11:24.81,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}对付中尉们\N{\fnArial\fs30}towards young subalterns.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.89,0:11:28.14,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但他是一步一步爬到这个位置的\N{\fnArial\fs30}But he'd clawed his way to the top, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.27,0:11:30.73,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}走到这步就必须变得残暴\N{\fnArial\fs30}you need to be ruthless to do that.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.85,0:11:32.23,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你肯定他作为司令官\N{\fnArial\fs30}Surely he didn't still feel{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.35,0:11:34.19,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}不觉得不适应？\N{\fnArial\fs30}out of place as an officer?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.31,0:11:36.15,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}不 我不这么认为\N{\fnArial\fs30}No, I don't think so, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.23,0:11:38.49,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但他被一种特殊的抑郁困扰着\N{\fnArial\fs30}but he was subject to a peculiar form of depression.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.07,0:11:43.95,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}敬女王\N{\fnArial\fs30}The Queen.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.67,0:11:59.63,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}有时在我们讨论以往的战役时\N{\fnArial\fs30}Sometimes when we were discussing old campaigns, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.72,0:12:03.59,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}总督 叛乱 阿富汗战争\N{\fnArial\fs30}the premier, the Mutiny, Afghan War, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.72,0:12:07.51,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他会突然笑意尽失\N{\fnArial\fs30}the smile would often be struck from his mouth{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.60,0:12:11.56,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}像被无形之手扯了下来\N{\fnArial\fs30}as if by some invisible hand.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.57,0:12:21.20,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是的 长期服役于印度\N{\fnArial\fs30}Yes, long service in India{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.28,0:12:23.20,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}会产生这种症状\N{\fnArial\fs30}can have that effect.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.28,0:12:25.57,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我在波克夏的时候见过\N{\fnArial\fs30}I saw that when I was in the Berkshires.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.70,0:12:28.20,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你提到一根木质棍子\N{\fnArial\fs30}You mentioned a carved wooden club{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.29,0:12:30.37,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}落在尸体旁\N{\fnArial\fs30}found by the body, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.45,0:12:33.67,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是上校自印度带回来的纪念品吗？\N{\fnArial\fs30}one of the Colonel's Indian souvenirs?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.75,0:12:35.21,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我相信仆人们会说\N{\fnArial\fs30}I believe the servants deny{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.29,0:12:37.71,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}从未见过这根棍子\N{\fnArial\fs30}ever having seen this club before.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.79,0:12:39.96,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}当然 我拜访时也从未见过\N{\fnArial\fs30}Certainly I've never seen it on any of my visits.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.09,0:12:42.26,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}它相当的长\N{\fnArial\fs30}It was quite long.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.38,0:12:44.26,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}那么警方 我猜\N{\fnArial\fs30}And the police, I suppose, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.38,0:12:46.01,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}有没有将其扣押检察？\N{\fnArial\fs30}have retained it for examination?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.09,0:12:47.47,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}有\N{\fnArial\fs30}Yes.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.60,0:12:49.43,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他们认为那就是凶器\N{\fnArial\fs30}They believe it to be the murder weapon.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.56,0:12:51.31,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他们这么认为？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Do they, indeed?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.43,0:12:53.14,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我想我们该首先\N{\fnArial\fs30}I think we should begin{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.27,0:12:55.06,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}动身去巴克利宅\N{\fnArial\fs30}by visiting the Barclays' house, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.15,0:12:56.69,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}不过首先 当然\N{\fnArial\fs30}unless, of course, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.77,0:12:59.48,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是否有可能与巴克利夫人面谈？\N{\fnArial\fs30}it is possible to interview Mrs. Barclay?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.61,0:13:03.65,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}恐怕她仍在昏迷之中\N{\fnArial\fs30}I'm afraid she's still unconscious.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.78,0:13:05.49,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}如我所料\N{\fnArial\fs30}I thought as much.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.62,0:13:17.75,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}大卫 大卫\N{\fnArial\fs30}David, David.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.94,0:13:32.19,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}多么美妙的早晨啊\N{\fnArial\fs30}What a beautiful morning.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.32,0:13:35.49,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}福尔摩斯 是不是巴克利夫人\N{\fnArial\fs30}Holmes, suppose Mrs. Barclay{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.61,0:13:39.99,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}红杏出墙 上校发现了？\N{\fnArial\fs30}had a lover and the Colonel had found out?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.11,0:13:43.91,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}墨斐少校看起来和她相当亲近\N{\fnArial\fs30}Major Murphy seems to have been rather close to her.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.99,0:13:47.21,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你知道 轻微的通奸行为\N{\fnArial\fs30}You know, mild adultery{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.33,0:13:48.87,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}一直是老生常谈\N{\fnArial\fs30}has always been commonplace{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.00,0:13:50.79,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}在热带军官夫妇间\N{\fnArial\fs30}among officers and their wives{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.88,0:13:53.13,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}时有发生\N{\fnArial\fs30}serving in hot climates.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.25,0:13:54.50,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}谢谢 华生\N{\fnArial\fs30}Thank you, Watson, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.63,0:13:57.34,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}教会了我军队里的道德\N{\fnArial\fs30}for educating me in military morality.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.47,0:13:58.88,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}如果真有什么特殊关系\N{\fnArial\fs30}If there had been anything{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.01,0:14:00.97,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}在墨斐少校和巴克利夫人之间\N{\fnArial\fs30}between Major Murphy and Mrs. Barclay, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.09,0:14:02.89,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他又怎么会提起\N{\fnArial\fs30}would he have related the incident{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.01,0:14:04.64,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}忘记雪茄盒这件事呢？\N{\fnArial\fs30}of his forgotten cigar case?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.52,0:14:55.27,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}大概是在7点半左右 先生\N{\fnArial\fs30}I was about half past seven, sir, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.40,0:14:57.40,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我在餐桌边等着\N{\fnArial\fs30}and I was waiting a table.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.53,0:14:58.90,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}巴克利夫人每月的那晚\N{\fnArial\fs30}Once a month, Mrs. Barclay spent{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.99,0:15:02.28,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}都要去奥尔德肖特做慈善事业\N{\fnArial\fs30}the evening doing charity work in Aldershot.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.11,0:15:41.53,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你这么着急是要去哪里？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Where are you off to in such a hurry?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.61,0:15:46.12,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}8点钟开始发放衣物\N{\fnArial\fs30}Well, the distribution of old clothing starts at 8 o'clock, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.24,0:15:48.49,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我向安·莫里森允诺过\N{\fnArial\fs30}and I promised Ann Morrison{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.62,0:15:51.58,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我会按时到达工作厅\N{\fnArial\fs30}I'd be at the mission hall on time.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.70,0:15:54.25,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}好吧 如果你想因此感染恶疾\N{\fnArial\fs30}Well, if you want to catch some filthy disease{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.37,0:15:57.29,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}上上下下沾满跳蚤的话\N{\fnArial\fs30}dealing with a lot of flea ridden down and outs, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.42,0:15:58.88,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我想那是你的事\N{\fnArial\fs30}I suppose that's your affair.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.96,0:16:00.55,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我深信人要懂得\N{\fnArial\fs30}I believe in putting back into life{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.63,0:16:03.05,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}知恩图报\N{\fnArial\fs30}as much as one gets out of it.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.13,0:16:07.43,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我们的命运如此幸运\N{\fnArial\fs30}We've been fortunate with our lot.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.55,0:16:13.98,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}其他人就没这么好运了\N{\fnArial\fs30}Others haven't been so lucky.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.06,0:16:15.98,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}别太晚回来\N{\fnArial\fs30}Don't be late back.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.06,0:16:18.65,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}当然不会\N{\fnArial\fs30}Of course not.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.79,0:16:32.45,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}巴克利夫人回来的时候\N{\fnArial\fs30}Mrs. Barclay must have returned{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.58,0:16:34.91,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}一定有9点一刻了 先生\N{\fnArial\fs30}about quarter past nine, sir.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.00,0:16:39.34,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我那时在厨房帮厨师洗盘子\N{\fnArial\fs30}I was in the kitchen helping the cook with the dishes.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.46,0:16:41.13,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}远处传来轰轰的雷声\N{\fnArial\fs30}There was thunder in the distance, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.21,0:16:43.13,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我正对范尼夫人说着\N{\fnArial\fs30}and I was just saying to Mrs. Fenning{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.21,0:16:45.09,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}暴风雨即将来临的时候\N{\fnArial\fs30}that there was a storm brewing, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.17,0:16:47.18,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}起居室有人拉铃\N{\fnArial\fs30}when the morning room bell rang.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.30,0:16:51.26,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我上楼后发现巴克利夫人已经归来\N{\fnArial\fs30}I came up here to find that Mrs. Barclay had returned.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.35,0:16:53.81,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}她在房间里来回踱步 先生\N{\fnArial\fs30}She was walking up and down this room, sir, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.89,0:17:00.82,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}面无血色 心烦意乱\N{\fnArial\fs30}very pale, upset.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.94,0:17:05.32,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}她看起来糟透了 先生\N{\fnArial\fs30}She looked awful, sir.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.33,0:17:12.79,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}您叫我 夫人？\N{\fnArial\fs30}You rang, madam?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.87,0:17:18.00,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是的 简 给我沏杯茶 好吗？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Yes, Jane, bring me some tea, will you?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.12,0:17:21.71,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}好的 夫人\N{\fnArial\fs30}Of course, madam.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.06,0:17:39.10,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}简 是你吗？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Jane, is that you?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.23,0:17:42.61,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是的 先生\N{\fnArial\fs30}Yes, sir.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.73,0:17:45.94,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我是否听到了巴克利夫人回来的声音？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Did I hear Mrs. Barclay come in?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.07,0:17:49.32,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是的 先生 她在起居室\N{\fnArial\fs30}Yes, sir, she's in the morning room.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.41,0:17:50.87,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}起居室？\N{\fnArial\fs30}The morning room?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.95,0:17:51.91,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是的 先生\N{\fnArial\fs30}Yes, sir.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.03,0:17:54.41,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我正准备去给她泡茶\N{\fnArial\fs30}I'm just about to take her a pot of tea.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.54,0:18:00.96,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}茶？这么晚了她喝茶做什么？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Tea? what does she want tea for at this hour?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.60,0:18:17.89,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我推测 这次\N{\fnArial\fs30}And that, presumably, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.02,0:18:21.35,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是最后有人见到活着的巴克利上校？\N{\fnArial\fs30}was the last time that anyone saw Colonel Barclay alive?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.44,0:18:24.69,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是的 先生\N{\fnArial\fs30}Yes, sir.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.77,0:18:27.15,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你能想到任何原因\N{\fnArial\fs30}Can you think of any reason{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.28,0:18:30.78,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}让你的女主人大半夜\N{\fnArial\fs30}why your mistress came into this morning room{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.91,0:18:34.28,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}走进没有炉火的起居室吗？\N{\fnArial\fs30}at that time of night, when the fire was unlit?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.41,0:18:35.87,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}不 先生\N{\fnArial\fs30}No, sir.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.95,0:18:37.75,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}她经常会出刻意\N{\fnArial\fs30}Did she often make a point{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.87,0:18:42.13,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}避开上校吗？\N{\fnArial\fs30}of purposely avoiding the Colonel?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.25,0:18:47.76,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你之前听到过他们争吵吗？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Had you ever heard them arguing before?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.84,0:18:53.14,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}据我所知没有 先生\N{\fnArial\fs30}Not to my knowledge, sir.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.26,0:18:54.97,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}当你从厨房回来\N{\fnArial\fs30}When you returned from the kitchen{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.10,0:18:57.14,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}端着巴克利夫人的茶\N{\fnArial\fs30}with Mrs. Barclay's tea, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.27,0:18:59.10,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你发现门被锁上了\N{\fnArial\fs30}you found the door locked, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.18,0:19:00.85,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你听到大声的争吵\N{\fnArial\fs30}and you heard voices raised.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.98,0:19:03.81,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你到底听到了什么？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Now, what exactly did you hear?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.94,0:19:08.57,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他们在争吵 先生\N{\fnArial\fs30}They were arguing, sir.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.65,0:19:11.86,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}巴克利夫人骂上校是个懦夫\N{\fnArial\fs30}Mrs. Barclay called the Colonel a coward.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.99,0:19:16.24,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}她说「这些年来你毁了我的一生」\N{\fnArial\fs30}She said you have ruined my life all these years.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.33,0:19:19.62,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}巴克利夫人大喊着「大卫」这个名字\N{\fnArial\fs30}Mrs. Barclay shouted the name "David, "{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.75,0:19:23.67,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}她喊了两次\N{\fnArial\fs30}she said it twice.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.79,0:19:25.84,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}大卫？\N{\fnArial\fs30}David?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.96,0:19:27.46,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你确定吗？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Could you swear to that?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.55,0:19:29.80,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我听得很清楚 先生\N{\fnArial\fs30}I was perfectly clear, sir.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.92,0:19:33.22,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但上校的名字是詹姆斯\N{\fnArial\fs30}But the Colonel's name was James.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.34,0:19:34.64,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你曾经听到\N{\fnArial\fs30}Have you ever heard{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.76,0:19:37.47,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}巴克利夫人提到过叫大卫的人吗？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Mrs. Barclay refer to anyone called David?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.60,0:19:40.02,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}没有 先生 我认为她和上校\N{\fnArial\fs30}No, sir, I don't think she or the Colonel{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.10,0:19:41.98,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}都不认识任何叫大卫的人\N{\fnArial\fs30}knew anyone by the name of David.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.06,0:19:46.69,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}墨斐少校的教名是帕特里克\N{\fnArial\fs30}And Major Murphy's christian name is Patrick.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.81,0:19:49.03,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他们最近有没有叫\N{\fnArial\fs30}Had they had any visitors recently{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.15,0:19:50.94,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}大卫的访客？\N{\fnArial\fs30}by the name of David?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.03,0:19:53.91,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我想没有 先生\N{\fnArial\fs30}I don't think so, sir.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.03,0:19:56.20,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}找到的那根棍子\N{\fnArial\fs30}The club that was found{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.32,0:19:58.83,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}扔在尸体旁边的\N{\fnArial\fs30}by Colonel Barclay's body, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.91,0:20:00.83,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你以前见过吗？\N{\fnArial\fs30}had you seen it before?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.91,0:20:02.41,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}没有 先生\N{\fnArial\fs30}No, sir.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.54,0:20:04.17,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}上校有很多印度带回来的战利品\N{\fnArial\fs30}The Colonel had several trophies from India, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.29,0:20:07.50,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但没有那根棍子\N{\fnArial\fs30}but nothing like that club.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.63,0:20:10.51,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你确定吗 斯图尔特小姐？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Are you sure of that, Miss Stewart?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.59,0:20:12.05,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是的 先生\N{\fnArial\fs30}Yes, sir.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.17,0:20:17.93,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我不知道它是从哪来的\N{\fnArial\fs30}I don't know where it came from.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.05,0:20:23.02,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}谢谢 我问完了\N{\fnArial\fs30}Thank you, that is all.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.14,0:20:26.48,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}哦 不 还有最后一个问题\N{\fnArial\fs30}Oh, no, there is just one last thing, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.56,0:20:28.65,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}墨斐少校落在这儿的雪茄盒\N{\fnArial\fs30}Major Murphy once left his cigar case here, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.73,0:20:31.03,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你找到了没有？\N{\fnArial\fs30}did you manage to find it?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.11,0:20:33.90,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}找到了 先生\N{\fnArial\fs30}Yes, sir.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.54,0:20:48.21,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}上校就躺在这里 先生\N{\fnArial\fs30}The Colonel was lying down here, sir.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.29,0:20:50.09,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}头抵着壁炉架？\N{\fnArial\fs30}With his head by the fender?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.21,0:20:52.21,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是的 先生\N{\fnArial\fs30}Yes, sir.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.30,0:20:56.13,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}血迹仍清晰可见\N{\fnArial\fs30}You can see the mark of the blood still.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.26,0:21:00.43,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但最恐怖的事 先生 是他的脸\N{\fnArial\fs30}But the most frightening thing of all, sir, was his face.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.56,0:21:01.93,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他的脸？\N{\fnArial\fs30}His face?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.02,0:21:03.81,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}当我把他翻过来时\N{\fnArial\fs30}When I rolled him over.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.93,0:21:07.90,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我一看差点吓晕过去\N{\fnArial\fs30}I almost fainted away to look upon it.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.98,0:21:12.28,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他的脸完全扭曲了 非常狰狞\N{\fnArial\fs30}It was all contorted, screwed up, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.40,0:21:17.20,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}带着恐惧到极点的表情\N{\fnArial\fs30}with the most horrible look of fear and terror.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.28,0:21:23.37,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}就像他预见到自己的死期一样？\N{\fnArial\fs30}As if he'd foreseen his own death?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.45,0:21:26.58,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}很有可能 先生\N{\fnArial\fs30}Quite possible, sir.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.71,0:21:31.29,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}谢谢你 贝茨\N{\fnArial\fs30}Thank you, Bates.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.42,0:21:34.30,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是什么幻影 什么鬼怪\N{\fnArial\fs30}What apparition, what monster was it{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.42,0:21:39.59,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}能让上校如此畏惧\N{\fnArial\fs30}that could have frightened the Colonel so.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.72,0:21:44.18,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}肯定不是南希·巴克利\N{\fnArial\fs30}Not Nancy Barclay, for sure.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.31,0:21:46.14,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}门被反锁了 先生\N{\fnArial\fs30}This door was locked shut, sir, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.27,0:21:51.15,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}而且 钥匙不见了\N{\fnArial\fs30}and what's more, the key was missing.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.27,0:21:53.02,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}不见了？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Missing?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.15,0:21:55.11,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是的 最后我们不得不\N{\fnArial\fs30}Yes, in the end we had to send{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.23,0:21:57.28,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}请锁匠来把门打开\N{\fnArial\fs30}for a locksmith to open it.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.36,0:21:59.61,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你们彻底找过那把钥匙吗？\N{\fnArial\fs30}You have made a thorough search for the key?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.70,0:22:01.24,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我们已经掘地三尺了\N{\fnArial\fs30}We searched high and low.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.32,0:22:02.87,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}巴克利夫人没拿着\N{\fnArial\fs30}Mrs. Barclay hadn't got it, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.99,0:22:05.16,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}也不在上校衣兜里 先生\N{\fnArial\fs30}and it wasn't in the Colonel's pocket, sir.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.29,0:22:10.96,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}多谢 范尼夫人\N{\fnArial\fs30}Thank you, Mrs. Fenning.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.08,0:22:17.13,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}华生 如果钥匙不在门上\N{\fnArial\fs30}Watson, if the key was not in the door, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.22,0:22:22.68,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}也不在巴克利夫人和上校身上 那么…\N{\fnArial\fs30}and neither Mrs. Barclay nor the Colonel had it, then…{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.80,0:22:28.43,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}屋里肯定有第三个人\N{\fnArial\fs30}Then there must have been a third person.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.52,0:22:35.19,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}完全正确\N{\fnArial\fs30}Exactly, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.32,0:22:45.58,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他从落地窗进来 或者出去\N{\fnArial\fs30}who either entered or left through those windows.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:51.71,0:22:59.26,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}这些是贝茨的脚印\N{\fnArial\fs30}These are Bates' footprints.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:59.38,0:23:03.18,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但这些 是另一个人的脚印\N{\fnArial\fs30}But these, are the footprints of someone else.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:03.30,0:23:07.31,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}有人最近穿越过草地\N{\fnArial\fs30}Someone has recently crossed this lawn, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:07.39,0:23:10.77,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}痕迹非常清晰\N{\fnArial\fs30}the marks are just visible.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:24.57,0:23:28.49,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他从落地窗进去 又原路出来 华生\N{\fnArial\fs30}He entered and left through those windows, Watson, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.58,0:23:30.71,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我们找对方向了\N{\fnArial\fs30}we're on the right search.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.96,0:23:41.92,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}华生 快看这个\N{\fnArial\fs30}Watson, look at this.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.01,0:23:43.55,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}这是什么？\N{\fnArial\fs30}What is it?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.68,0:23:46.43,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我们的对手有个不太寻常的伙伴\N{\fnArial\fs30}Our entrant had a somewhat unusual companion.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.55,0:23:49.10,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是只狗 对吧？有个人养狗\N{\fnArial\fs30}It's a dog, isn't it, somebody's dog?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.22,0:23:50.81,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}哪有人听说过会\N{\fnArial\fs30}Whoever heard of a dog{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.93,0:23:52.52,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}爬上床帘的狗\N{\fnArial\fs30}running up a curtain.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.60,0:23:54.40,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}那是不是猫？\N{\fnArial\fs30}What about a cat then?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:54.52,0:23:56.52,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}这些爪印不是猫的\N{\fnArial\fs30}These claw marks are not those of a cat, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:56.61,0:23:58.48,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}也不是猴子 或是任何一种\N{\fnArial\fs30}nor of a monkey, nor of any creature{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.61,0:24:00.74,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我们熟悉的生物\N{\fnArial\fs30}that we are familiar with.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:00.82,0:24:04.91,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我想前后蹄之间的距离\N{\fnArial\fs30}I would think from hind foot to forefoot{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:05.03,0:24:08.08,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}至少有15英寸\N{\fnArial\fs30}at least 15 inches.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:08.16,0:24:10.24,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}加上头颈的长度\N{\fnArial\fs30}Add to that the length of neck and head, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.33,0:24:13.16,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}这个动物不少于两英尺长\N{\fnArial\fs30}you have a creature no less than two feet, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:13.29,0:24:15.42,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}加上尾巴就更长\N{\fnArial\fs30}more if there's a tail.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:15.50,0:24:17.46,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}它的步幅很奇特\N{\fnArial\fs30}The length of its stride is odd, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:17.59,0:24:20.00,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}这暗示着它\N{\fnArial\fs30}it indicates a creature{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:20.13,0:24:22.38,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}背部修长 腿部短小\N{\fnArial\fs30}with a long back and short legs.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:22.47,0:24:24.68,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}像鼬或黄鼠狼之类的动物？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Something like a stoat or a weasel?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:24.80,0:24:27.89,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}同时我们知道它是食肉动物\N{\fnArial\fs30}We also know that it is carnivorous.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:27.97,0:24:30.10,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你怎么看出来的？\N{\fnArial\fs30}How can you tell that?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:30.18,0:24:35.27,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你看看它爬上床帘是为什么\N{\fnArial\fs30}Well you see what made it run up the curtain.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:35.35,0:24:36.85,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}金丝雀\N{\fnArial\fs30}The canary.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:36.98,0:24:38.98,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}正是\N{\fnArial\fs30}Exactly.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:39.11,0:24:41.19,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}到底是什么动物？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Then what was this beast?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:50.08,0:24:54.04,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}不 我不能 我不能背叛我的朋友\N{\fnArial\fs30}No, I can't, I cannot betray a friend, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:54.16,0:24:57.54,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}请不要逼我\N{\fnArial\fs30}please don't ask me to.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:12.77,0:25:14.68,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}莫里森小姐\N{\fnArial\fs30}Miss Morrison, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:14.77,0:25:21.11,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}当巴克利夫人前日晚来到这里时\N{\fnArial\fs30}when Mrs. Barclay left her house to come here two nights ago, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:21.19,0:25:25.65,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}她很快乐而满足\N{\fnArial\fs30}she was happy and content.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:25.74,0:25:27.24,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但两小时后 她回去的时候\N{\fnArial\fs30}When she returned two hours later, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:27.36,0:25:28.66,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}却完全变了样\N{\fnArial\fs30}she was a changed woman.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:28.78,0:25:33.91,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}现在警方怀疑她是凶手\N{\fnArial\fs30}Now the police suspect her of murder.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:34.04,0:25:38.33,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你有责任澄清你朋友的名声\N{\fnArial\fs30}You owe it to your friend to clear her name.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:38.46,0:25:40.67,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你必须告诉我那晚什么事\N{\fnArial\fs30}You must tell me what happened last night{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:40.79,0:25:44.01,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}彻底改变了她\N{\fnArial\fs30}that so changed her.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:44.09,0:25:49.43,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}很好 我愿意打破沉默\N{\fnArial\fs30}Very well, I shall break my promise of silence{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:49.55,0:25:53.39,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}如果真能对她有所帮助\N{\fnArial\fs30}if what I can say can really help her.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:53.51,0:25:56.68,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}的确有事发生\N{\fnArial\fs30}So there was something.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:56.81,0:26:00.23,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}事情十分异乎寻常\N{\fnArial\fs30}It was most bizarre.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:00.31,0:26:02.07,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我得说我们在这儿见过\N{\fnArial\fs30}I should explain that we come across{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:02.19,0:26:05.99,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}各种各样穷困潦倒的人\N{\fnArial\fs30}all sorts of conditions of men here.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:06.07,0:26:07.45,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}然而 那一晚\N{\fnArial\fs30}Yet, the other night, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:07.57,0:26:09.53,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我看到了从未见过的\N{\fnArial\fs30}I saw the most extraordinary creature{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:09.61,0:26:12.70,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}最奇特的一位\N{\fnArial\fs30}I have ever seen.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:12.83,0:26:16.62,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他不仅驼背\N{\fnArial\fs30}Not only had he a crooked back, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:16.75,0:26:18.87,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}脚还是跛的\N{\fnArial\fs30}but he was lame{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:19.00,0:26:22.50,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}走路时曲着膝盖\N{\fnArial\fs30}and walked with his knees bent.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:22.59,0:26:25.09,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他面色黧黑\N{\fnArial\fs30}His face was darkly tanned, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:25.21,0:26:28.13,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}干瘪褶皱得像烂苹果一样\N{\fnArial\fs30}crinkled and puckered like a withered apple.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:28.26,0:26:29.80,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}那时我想 果真\N{\fnArial\fs30}I thought to myself that truly{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:29.93,0:26:31.72,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}这世上还有如此\N{\fnArial\fs30}there are some of us on this earth{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:31.80,0:26:33.72,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}不堪重负\N{\fnArial\fs30}who are burdened with more than{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:33.81,0:26:36.85,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}被命运遗弃的人\N{\fnArial\fs30}their fair share of misfortune.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:36.93,0:26:39.44,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}更显得奇异的是\N{\fnArial\fs30}This vision was made more unusual{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:39.56,0:26:47.24,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}那人还一身东方打扮\N{\fnArial\fs30}by the oriental garb the man was wearing.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:47.32,0:26:51.41,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我指给南希看\N{\fnArial\fs30}I pointed this person out to Nancy{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:51.49,0:26:58.87,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}那个人似乎特别需要帮助\N{\fnArial\fs30}as someone especially deserving of help.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:58.96,0:27:02.63,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}南希那晚精神很不错\N{\fnArial\fs30}Nancy had indeed been in good spirits that evening, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:02.75,0:27:04.09,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我看到她走近那个男人\N{\fnArial\fs30}and I saw her go towards the man{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:04.17,0:27:12.01,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}询问他是否需要照顾\N{\fnArial\fs30}and ask him if he needed assistance.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:12.14,0:27:16.26,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}就是这时候 南希起了变化\N{\fnArial\fs30}It was now that a change came over Nancy.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:16.39,0:27:18.73,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}她与那个男人谈了几句\N{\fnArial\fs30}She had begun a conversation with the man when suddenly{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:18.81,0:27:22.10,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}脸色骤然苍白\N{\fnArial\fs30}all the color drained from her face.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:22.19,0:27:25.61,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}看起来像见鬼了似的\N{\fnArial\fs30}She looked as though she had seen a ghost.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:25.69,0:27:27.98,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}那个男人似乎也受到很大影响\N{\fnArial\fs30}The man, too, seemed to be strangely affected{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:28.11,0:27:29.94,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}见到她的脸\N{\fnArial\fs30}by the sight of her, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:30.03,0:27:33.11,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我见他不断使劲挥手\N{\fnArial\fs30}and I saw him gesticulating wildly.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:33.24,0:27:35.95,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}然后 南希和那男人在大厅\N{\fnArial\fs30}Well, Nancy and the man went to a quiet corner{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:36.08,0:27:38.75,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}找了个安静角落谈话\N{\fnArial\fs30}of the hall and they talked together{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:38.83,0:27:40.16,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}谈了一些时候\N{\fnArial\fs30}for a few moments or so{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:40.29,0:27:42.46,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我听到那个男人一声怒吼\N{\fnArial\fs30}before I heard an angry shout from the man{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:42.54,0:27:47.25,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}接着看到他挥舞着拳头 冲出门去\N{\fnArial\fs30}and saw him storm out, waving his fists in the air.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:59.52,0:28:01.89,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}南希 怎么了\N{\fnArial\fs30}Nancy, what is it, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:02.02,0:28:04.65,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你还好吧？\N{\fnArial\fs30}are you all right?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:04.73,0:28:07.82,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}那个可怜的家伙是谁？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Who was that poor creature?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:07.94,0:28:09.78,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是我的一个旧相识\N{\fnArial\fs30}It's an old acquaintance of mine{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:09.86,0:28:13.28,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}现在落魄了\N{\fnArial\fs30}fallen on hard times.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:13.36,0:28:15.07,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}答应我 安妮 你不会把这事\N{\fnArial\fs30}Promise me, Annie, you won't say anything{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:15.20,0:28:17.99,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}告诉任何人 答应我\N{\fnArial\fs30}about this to anyone, promise me.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:18.12,0:28:26.79,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}当然 我答应 只要是你的要求\N{\fnArial\fs30}Of course, I promise, if you so wish.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:26.88,0:28:30.30,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}那这个男人的身份呢？\N{\fnArial\fs30}And the identity of this man?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:30.38,0:28:33.30,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我猜你就会这么问\N{\fnArial\fs30}I thought you might ask me that.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:33.38,0:28:37.22,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}这件可怕的事发生之后 南希离开了\N{\fnArial\fs30}Well, after this terrible happening, Nancy left.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:37.35,0:28:39.10,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我自然去问了问\N{\fnArial\fs30}I naturally made a few inquiries{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:39.22,0:28:41.14,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}常来的那些人\N{\fnArial\fs30}among some of the regulars.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:41.22,0:28:43.89,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}如此与众不同的人\N{\fnArial\fs30}Such an unusual looking creature{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:44.02,0:28:46.73,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}当然很引人注意\N{\fnArial\fs30}has of course attracted attention.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:46.85,0:28:50.82,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}原来他是最近从印度回来的老兵\N{\fnArial\fs30}It appears he is an old soldier recently back from India, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:50.90,0:28:52.57,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}谁也不熟悉\N{\fnArial\fs30}and no one knows anything else{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:52.69,0:28:54.45,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他的身世背景\N{\fnArial\fs30}about his background{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:54.57,0:28:56.41,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}只知道他是靠\N{\fnArial\fs30}except that he makes a living{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:56.53,0:28:59.66,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}给部队逗乐 变戏法\N{\fnArial\fs30}by entertaining the troops, conjuring tricks, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:59.74,0:29:03.96,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}之类手段谋生\N{\fnArial\fs30}that kind of thing.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:04.08,0:29:08.96,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你对警方提到他了吗？\N{\fnArial\fs30}And did you tell the police about him?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:09.09,0:29:16.84,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}当然没有 一诺千金\N{\fnArial\fs30}Of course not, a promise is a promise.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:16.93,0:29:19.55,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是的 当然\N{\fnArial\fs30}Yes, of course.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:19.64,0:29:22.39,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}非常感谢 莫里森小姐\N{\fnArial\fs30}Thank you, Miss Morrison.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:55.73,0:30:59.78,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}那就是闯入者的四足小伙伴\N{\fnArial\fs30}That is our intruder's four-footed companion.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:59.86,0:31:02.12,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是只猫鼬\N{\fnArial\fs30}It's a mongoose.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:02.20,0:31:06.33,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我想我们找到正主了\N{\fnArial\fs30}I think we've found our man.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:16.34,0:31:18.42,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我想您就是在印度服役过的亨利· 伍德先生\N{\fnArial\fs30}Mr. Henry Wood, I believe, late of India.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:18.55,0:31:19.92,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}能和您谈谈吗？\N{\fnArial\fs30}May I have a word?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:20.05,0:31:21.13,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}谈什么？\N{\fnArial\fs30}What about?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:21.22,0:31:26.14,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}关于詹姆斯·巴克利上校被杀一事\N{\fnArial\fs30}A little matter of Colonel James Barclay's death.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:57.44,0:32:01.11,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}她是无辜的 这点你得相信我\N{\fnArial\fs30}She's innocent, you can take my word for it.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:01.23,0:32:02.61,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}那么你是有罪的\N{\fnArial\fs30}Then you are guilty.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:02.73,0:32:06.57,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}不 我没罪\N{\fnArial\fs30}No, I am not guilty.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:06.65,0:32:10.20,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}那么是谁击倒上校的？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Then who struck the Colonel down?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:10.28,0:32:12.87,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是上天杀了他\N{\fnArial\fs30}It was a just Providence that killed him, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:12.95,0:32:15.91,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他自己不堪良心重负\N{\fnArial\fs30}his own guilty conscience.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:16.00,0:32:18.58,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我想你最好解释清楚\N{\fnArial\fs30}I think you'd better explain.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:18.71,0:32:21.83,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}天啊 如果是我打碎他的脑壳\N{\fnArial\fs30}My God, if I had smashed his head in, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:21.96,0:32:23.25,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}像我企盼已久的那样\N{\fnArial\fs30}as it was in my heart to do, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:23.38,0:32:29.05,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}那也是他欠我的\N{\fnArial\fs30}he would have got only what he deserved from me.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:29.13,0:32:33.93,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}不 我没碰过他一根手指头\N{\fnArial\fs30}No, I never laid a hand on him, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:34.06,0:32:40.19,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}根本不劳我动手\N{\fnArial\fs30}I was spared the trouble.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:40.31,0:32:44.69,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}让我讲讲我的故事\N{\fnArial\fs30}I'll tell you my story.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:44.82,0:32:54.12,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我对此丝毫不感到耻辱\N{\fnArial\fs30}There is no cause for me to be ashamed of it.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:56.20,0:33:02.67,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你们看到现在的我 背驼得像骆驼\N{\fnArial\fs30}You see me now with my back like a camel, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:02.79,0:33:06.50,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}肋骨也七扭八歪\N{\fnArial\fs30}my ribs all awry, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:06.63,0:33:09.80,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但从前的亨利·伍德下士\N{\fnArial\fs30}but there was a time when Corporal Henry Wood{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:09.88,0:33:14.93,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}可是麦洛斯团最潇洒的人\N{\fnArial\fs30}was the smartest man in the Royal Mallows.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:15.01,0:33:19.52,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你和巴克利上校同属一个团？\N{\fnArial\fs30}You were in the same regiment as Colonel Barclay?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:19.64,0:33:28.36,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}哦 是的 但那是他还是吉姆·巴克利中士\N{\fnArial\fs30}Oh, yes, but he was Sergeant Jim Barclay then.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:28.48,0:33:31.90,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我们同属一个连\N{\fnArial\fs30}We were in the same company, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:32.03,0:33:38.33,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我们还有另一个相同点\N{\fnArial\fs30}and we had something else in common, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:38.45,0:33:41.12,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}都深深爱着\N{\fnArial\fs30}we were both in love{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:41.21,0:33:47.17,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}同一个女人 南希·迪威艾\N{\fnArial\fs30}with the same woman, Nancy Devoy.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:47.30,0:33:48.55,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}她父亲是\N{\fnArial\fs30}Who was the daughter{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:48.67,0:33:53.43,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}团部军士长\N{\fnArial\fs30}of the Regimental Sergeant Major.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:53.55,0:33:59.47,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}两个男人深爱着她\N{\fnArial\fs30}There were two men who loved her, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:59.56,0:34:09.48,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但她只爱其中的一个\N{\fnArial\fs30}but only one whom she loved.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:15.28,0:34:19.87,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}她… 你们一定觉得可笑吧\N{\fnArial\fs30}She you'll laugh when you look at{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:19.95,0:34:25.21,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}这炉火前蜷缩的可怜虫\N{\fnArial\fs30}this poor thing huddled in front of the fire{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:25.29,0:34:34.88,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}敢自称是我英俊的外表\N{\fnArial\fs30}and hear me say that it was for my good looks{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:35.01,0:34:42.68,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}赢得了南希的爱\N{\fnArial\fs30}that Nancy loved me.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:55.78,0:35:00.12,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}她一直以来爱的是我\N{\fnArial\fs30}I was the one she loved all along.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:00.24,0:35:02.08,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但尽管我占据了她的心\N{\fnArial\fs30}But although I had her heart, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:02.16,0:35:09.42,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}她父亲却不赞成\N{\fnArial\fs30}her father didn't approve of me.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:09.54,0:35:13.09,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我虽然是个不拘小节 有些鲁莽的人\N{\fnArial\fs30}I was a harum-scarum, reckless sort of lad, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:13.21,0:35:18.97,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但我同时也是忠心耿耿 非常坦率\N{\fnArial\fs30}but I was always honest and plain dealing as well.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:19.10,0:35:25.85,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}哦 南希的父亲希望她嫁给巴克利\N{\fnArial\fs30}Oh, Nancy's father wanted her to marry Barclay.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:25.98,0:35:28.10,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他谨言慎行\N{\fnArial\fs30}He was careful to keep out of trouble, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:28.19,0:35:33.69,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}总是见机行事\N{\fnArial\fs30}always did the right thing, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:33.82,0:35:35.82,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}不像我这样 常带南希\N{\fnArial\fs30}not like me who took Nancy{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:35.95,0:35:39.28,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}去他父亲不喜欢的地方\N{\fnArial\fs30}to places her father didn't like.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:39.41,0:35:42.58,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}此外 巴克利受过教育\N{\fnArial\fs30}Besides, Barclay had had an education, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:42.66,0:35:45.29,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}就快要升为军官了\N{\fnArial\fs30}he was already marked for the sword-belt.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:45.37,0:35:47.50,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}迪威艾自然觉得巴克利\N{\fnArial\fs30}RSM Devoy naturally thought Barclay{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:47.62,0:35:55.34,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}和他女儿才是门当户对\N{\fnArial\fs30}the better match for his daughter.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:55.47,0:35:58.68,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但她对我真心实意\N{\fnArial\fs30}But she remained true to me, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:58.80,0:36:00.14,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我们本来要结婚了\N{\fnArial\fs30}and we would have married{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:00.22,0:36:02.60,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}如果不是那场暴动的话\N{\fnArial\fs30}had it not been for the Mutiny.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:02.68,0:36:07.52,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}为什么南希·迪威艾没嫁给所爱之人？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Why did Nancy Devoy not marry the man she loved?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:07.64,0:36:11.44,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}那是1857的雨季\N{\fnArial\fs30}It was monsoon time in 1857, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:11.52,0:36:15.32,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}当印度土兵对英国宣战之时\N{\fnArial\fs30}when the Sepoys rose up against the British.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:15.44,0:36:20.07,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我们团在伯第被狙击\N{\fnArial\fs30}The regiment was shut up in Bhurtee.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:20.20,0:36:22.66,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}一万多叛军把我们团团围住\N{\fnArial\fs30}There were 10, 000 rebels round us, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:22.78,0:36:26.79,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}密不透风 铁桶一般\N{\fnArial\fs30}pinning us down like terriers round a rat cage.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:26.87,0:36:29.37,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我们渐渐弹尽粮绝\N{\fnArial\fs30}We'd run short of food and ammunition, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:29.50,0:36:31.79,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}必须联系上尼尔将军正向\N{\fnArial\fs30}we had to communicate with General Neill's column{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:31.88,0:36:34.63,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}内地进军的纵队\N{\fnArial\fs30}that was moving up-country.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:34.71,0:36:37.59,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}这是唯一的获救方法\N{\fnArial\fs30}It was our only chance to get help.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:43.22,0:36:45.56,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我们连的司令官希望有志愿者\N{\fnArial\fs30}Our company commander had asked for a volunteer, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:45.68,0:36:48.48,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}一个机灵强壮的战士潜出营地\N{\fnArial\fs30}a fit, strong soldier to slip out of the garrison{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:48.56,0:36:50.40,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}趁着夜色通风报信\N{\fnArial\fs30}at dead of night and make contact{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:50.52,0:36:53.48,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}找到平原上的救援纵队\N{\fnArial\fs30}with the relief column out on the plain beyond.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:53.56,0:36:56.99,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}像傻子一样 我主动请缨\N{\fnArial\fs30}Like a fool, I volunteered.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:57.07,0:36:59.15,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}那是个危险重重的任务\N{\fnArial\fs30}It was a dangerous mission all right, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:59.24,0:37:02.87,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}千百条生命处于危险之中\N{\fnArial\fs30}there were a 1, 000 lives in peril.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:02.99,0:37:06.29,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但我只牵挂其中的一个…\N{\fnArial\fs30}But I was thinking of only one of them…{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:19.09,0:37:21.38,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}南希·迪威艾\N{\fnArial\fs30}Nancy Devoy, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:21.47,0:37:23.55,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我深爱的女人 世上最美丽\N{\fnArial\fs30}the woman I loved, and the finest girl{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:23.64,0:37:27.60,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}最生机勃勃的女人\N{\fnArial\fs30}that ever had the breath of life between her lips.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:27.68,0:37:35.57,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}和她道别是最难的一环\N{\fnArial\fs30}Saying goodbye to her was the hardest thing.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:35.65,0:37:39.74,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我们交换了定情信物 没想到\N{\fnArial\fs30}As we exchanged mementos, I never thought that{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:39.82,0:37:42.86,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}这一别就是30年\N{\fnArial\fs30}I was saying goodbye to her for 30 years.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:45.99,0:37:48.16,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是我追求南希的情敌\N{\fnArial\fs30}It was my rival for Nancy's hand{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:48.29,0:37:49.87,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}送我上的路\N{\fnArial\fs30}who saw me off on my journey{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:49.95,0:37:51.87,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}深夜穿越敌军封锁线\N{\fnArial\fs30}through the enemy lines that night, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:51.96,0:37:54.04,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}巴克利中士\N{\fnArial\fs30}Sergeant Barclay.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:54.13,0:37:55.63,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他说他对驻地\N{\fnArial\fs30}He said he knew the lie of the land{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:55.75,0:37:57.71,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}周边地形再清楚不过\N{\fnArial\fs30}around the garrison better than any other.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:57.80,0:38:00.05,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}当我志愿寻找救援的时候\N{\fnArial\fs30}While I volunteered to make the journey, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:00.13,0:38:02.34,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}吉姆·巴克利自愿指引我\N{\fnArial\fs30}Jim Barclay volunteered to advise me{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:02.47,0:38:06.76,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}最佳行动路径\N{\fnArial\fs30}on the best route to take.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:12.77,0:38:14.60,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}那之后\N{\fnArial\fs30}So, just after then, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:14.69,0:38:17.32,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}在战友的炮火掩护下\N{\fnArial\fs30}while my comrades gave me covering fire, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:17.44,0:38:20.90,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我出发了\N{\fnArial\fs30}I set off.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:24.57,0:38:26.49,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}巴克利告诉我沿着溪流\N{\fnArial\fs30}Barclay had told me to follow a stream{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:26.62,0:38:28.12,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}向一个小峡谷走\N{\fnArial\fs30}which would lead to a gully.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:28.24,0:38:31.70,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他说 这是最安全的下山途径\N{\fnArial\fs30}This, he said, was the safest way downhill.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:31.83,0:38:33.29,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他的指引很有用\N{\fnArial\fs30}His directions were perfect{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:33.41,0:38:35.21,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我很快就涉过刺骨的河水\N{\fnArial\fs30}and soon I was wading through icy water{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:35.33,0:38:40.30,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}那里昨天还是喜马拉雅山脉的积雪\N{\fnArial\fs30}that only the day before had been snow in the Himalayas.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:47.89,0:38:50.97,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我能看到叛军的营帐和灯火\N{\fnArial\fs30}I could see the lights and fires in the rebels' camp{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:51.06,0:38:52.60,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但我隐藏得很好\N{\fnArial\fs30}but I kept well down, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:52.68,0:38:54.98,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}躲过了哨兵的视线\N{\fnArial\fs30}out of sight of their sentry posts.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:55.10,0:38:57.81,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我到了小峡谷后 自认为安全了\N{\fnArial\fs30}I came to the gully and thought I was safe.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:04.15,0:39:07.16,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}紧接着 我被袭击了\N{\fnArial\fs30}Then it happened, I was attacked.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:07.28,0:39:09.58,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}重物击中了我的头部\N{\fnArial\fs30}Something hard cracked down on my head{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:09.70,0:39:15.42,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}之后就不省人事了\N{\fnArial\fs30}and everything spun around.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:15.54,0:39:19.46,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}当我醒来之后 我被绑得像只鸡一样\N{\fnArial\fs30}When I came to, I was trussed up like a chicken{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:19.54,0:39:21.80,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}还被挂在树上\N{\fnArial\fs30}and hanging from a tree.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:21.88,0:39:24.17,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我的手臂像是生生从\N{\fnArial\fs30}My arms felt as though they were being wrenched{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:24.26,0:39:26.93,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}关节处扯了开来\N{\fnArial\fs30}out of their sockets.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:27.05,0:39:30.26,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我不在乎疼痛 我最痛心的\N{\fnArial\fs30}I didn't mind the pain, but I was sick at heart{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:30.39,0:39:33.14,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是没能完成任务\N{\fnArial\fs30}for having failed in my mission.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:33.22,0:39:35.31,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}那些等待救助的人\N{\fnArial\fs30}What would be the fate of those{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:35.39,0:39:38.02,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他们的命运会如何呢？\N{\fnArial\fs30}I had been trying to save?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:47.91,0:39:50.03,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但最大的震惊是 从我能听懂的\N{\fnArial\fs30}But the biggest blow came as I listened{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:50.16,0:39:54.08,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}叛军口中说出的一些字眼\N{\fnArial\fs30}to what I could understand of a rebels' talk.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:54.20,0:39:57.87,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我发现自己被出卖了\N{\fnArial\fs30}I heard enough to realize that I had been betrayed.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:57.96,0:40:00.04,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}指引我方向的那个人\N{\fnArial\fs30}The very man who had shown me the way to take{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:00.17,0:40:02.46,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}居然把我出卖给敌人\N{\fnArial\fs30}had betrayed me to the enemy.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:02.59,0:40:04.63,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}巴克利不惜除掉我\N{\fnArial\fs30}Barclay had got rid of me{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:04.76,0:40:07.22,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}只为得到我的女孩\N{\fnArial\fs30}to make sure he could have my girl.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:14.14,0:40:22.15,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}现在 你们知道了詹姆斯·巴克利的心狠手辣\N{\fnArial\fs30}Now, you know what James Barclay was capable of.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:22.27,0:40:26.78,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}原来尼尔将军的纵队\N{\fnArial\fs30}Well, it turned out that General Neill's column{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:26.90,0:40:30.37,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}已经在救援伯第的路上了\N{\fnArial\fs30}was already on its way to relieve Bhurtee.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:30.45,0:40:32.87,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}叛军撤退了\N{\fnArial\fs30}The rebels retreated, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:32.95,0:40:36.20,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他们带走了我\N{\fnArial\fs30}they dragged me away with them.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:36.29,0:40:38.41,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}百般折磨我\N{\fnArial\fs30}I was tortured.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:38.50,0:40:45.13,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我试图逃跑 又被抓住折磨\N{\fnArial\fs30}I tried to escape, I was tortured again.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:45.25,0:40:48.09,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}又隔了多少年啊\N{\fnArial\fs30}It was to be many a long year{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:48.17,0:40:51.01,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我才再次看到一张白人的脸\N{\fnArial\fs30}before I saw another white face.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:56.52,0:40:59.98,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}俘虏我的人逃向北方 进入了深山\N{\fnArial\fs30}My captors fled north, further into the hills, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:00.10,0:41:03.19,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}把我当做奴隶\N{\fnArial\fs30}and used me as a sort of slave.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:03.31,0:41:04.90,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我过着猪狗不如的生活\N{\fnArial\fs30}I was treated worse than a dog{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:04.98,0:41:09.53,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}这些混蛋几乎折断了我每一根骨头\N{\fnArial\fs30}and they damn near broke every bone in my body.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:09.65,0:41:13.37,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}有时我更希望他们杀了我\N{\fnArial\fs30}Sometimes I'd wish they'd just killed me, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:13.49,0:41:15.62,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但我对那个毁我一生的人的厌恶\N{\fnArial\fs30}but my thoughts of hatred and loathing for the man{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:15.70,0:41:18.45,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}和仇恨支撑着我\N{\fnArial\fs30}who destroyed my life kept me going.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:18.54,0:41:22.63,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我每天都想着报复巴克利\N{\fnArial\fs30}I dreamed of revenge on Barclay.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:37.35,0:41:39.27,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}一天 阿富汗部落的人\N{\fnArial\fs30}One day some Afghan tribesmen{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:39.35,0:41:42.27,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}杀死了看守我的叛军\N{\fnArial\fs30}murdered the rebels that held me prisoner.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:42.35,0:41:44.36,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}把我留在那儿自生自灭\N{\fnArial\fs30}They left me for dead, too.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:44.48,0:41:47.44,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但奇迹发生了 我依旧活着\N{\fnArial\fs30}But by a miracle, I still lived.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:55.33,0:41:59.00,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}于是 我像对向那些对我施暴的人复仇\N{\fnArial\fs30}So, I had my revenge on my torturers, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:59.12,0:42:02.54,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但巴克利早就不知去向\N{\fnArial\fs30}but Barclay was beyond my grasp.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:02.67,0:42:04.58,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}至于南希\N{\fnArial\fs30}And what of Nancy, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:04.71,0:42:07.00,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我不知她是生是死\N{\fnArial\fs30}I had no means of knowing whether she was alive or dead.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:12.05,0:42:14.34,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我流浪回到旁遮普\N{\fnArial\fs30}I wandered back to the Punjab, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:14.47,0:42:16.64,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}住在土人中间\N{\fnArial\fs30}and lived among the natives, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:16.72,0:42:19.22,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}靠耍些把戏为生\N{\fnArial\fs30}picking up a living by the conjuring tricks{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:19.31,0:42:21.98,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我跟随街头魔术师学了不少\N{\fnArial\fs30}I'd learned from the street magicians.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:22.06,0:42:24.94,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}何必奢望呢 我一个瘸子\N{\fnArial\fs30}What use was it for me, a wretched cripple, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:25.06,0:42:28.02,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}就算乘船回到英格兰\N{\fnArial\fs30}to get passage back by ship to England{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:28.11,0:42:32.40,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}和团里的老战友重聚 又有什么用？\N{\fnArial\fs30}and make myself known to my old comrades in the regiment?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:32.53,0:42:38.03,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}向吉姆·巴克利复仇的怒焰也没能让我这么做\N{\fnArial\fs30}Even revenge on Jim Barclay didn't make me go.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:38.16,0:42:42.21,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}不 我… 直说吧\N{\fnArial\fs30}No, I I'll tell you straight, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:42.33,0:42:44.92,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我更希望我的南希和麦洛斯团的\N{\fnArial\fs30}I preferred my Nancy and my old pals{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:45.04,0:42:48.21,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}老战友们继续相信\N{\fnArial\fs30}in the Royal Mallows to go on believing{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:48.34,0:42:51.42,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}亨利·伍德已经英勇牺牲\N{\fnArial\fs30}that Harry Wood died a hero's death{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:51.55,0:42:53.68,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}直着腰杆而死\N{\fnArial\fs30}with a straight back, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:53.76,0:42:57.18,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}不愿让他们看我屈膝弓背\N{\fnArial\fs30}than see him crawling about the world{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:57.26,0:43:04.85,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}像猩猩一样爬行 不成人形\N{\fnArial\fs30}more like a chimpanzee than a human being.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:04.94,0:43:06.90,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但你还是回来了\N{\fnArial\fs30}But you did return, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:06.98,0:43:10.53,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}回到你团部驻扎的奥尔德肖特 为什么？\N{\fnArial\fs30}and to Aldershot where your old regiment was stationed, why?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:10.61,0:43:15.24,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我只想在死前再看看故乡\N{\fnArial\fs30}I just wanted to see the old country once more before I died.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:15.36,0:43:24.50,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我省吃俭用 终于坐船出发了\N{\fnArial\fs30}I saved what I could and eventually I got a ship.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:24.62,0:43:33.88,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我不知道团部仍驻扎在奥尔德肖特\N{\fnArial\fs30}I didn't know the regiment was stationed here in Aldershot, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:33.97,0:43:36.63,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我只想回到战士们的驻地\N{\fnArial\fs30}I just wanted to be where there were soldiers.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:36.76,0:43:39.10,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我可以到各处的餐厅讨生活\N{\fnArial\fs30}I could earn my keep going around the canteens{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:39.22,0:43:43.85,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}变戏法逗他们乐\N{\fnArial\fs30}doing my tricks to entertain them.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:43.98,0:43:47.60,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我不再想杀了巴克利\N{\fnArial\fs30}I no longer wanted to kill Barclay, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:47.73,0:43:49.61,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}复仇之火\N{\fnArial\fs30}the fires of revenge{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:49.73,0:43:56.11,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}在时间的历练下已所剩无几\N{\fnArial\fs30}had burned low over the years…{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:56.20,0:44:04.08,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}直到我见到她\N{\fnArial\fs30}until I saw her.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:13.30,0:44:15.67,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我觉得我应该更英国化些\N{\fnArial\fs30}I thought I'd better get some English tongs, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:15.80,0:44:17.97,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我已经很滑稽了\N{\fnArial\fs30}I looked comical enough without wearing{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:18.05,0:44:20.89,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}不能再穿这些异国的衣服\N{\fnArial\fs30}these foreign clothes the whole time.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:21.01,0:44:23.35,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}起先 我专心致志挑一件\N{\fnArial\fs30}At first, I was more interested in finding{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:23.47,0:44:25.81,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}厚点的外套 不大在乎\N{\fnArial\fs30}a thick overcoat than looking at the charity{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:25.89,0:44:28.85,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}分发物品的慈善女士们\N{\fnArial\fs30}ladies who were doling them out.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:28.94,0:44:33.69,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}之后她们中的一个走过来\N{\fnArial\fs30}Then one of them came over, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:33.82,0:44:38.28,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我立刻认出了她\N{\fnArial\fs30}I recognized her at once, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:38.36,0:44:44.54,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}她几乎没变 还是那么漂亮\N{\fnArial\fs30}she'd hardly changed, still beautiful.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:44.66,0:44:47.62,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}更令我惊奇的是她…\N{\fnArial\fs30}What's more amazing is she…{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:47.71,0:44:51.46,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}她好像认识我\N{\fnArial\fs30}she seemed to know me.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:51.54,0:44:53.34,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}晚上好 我能帮助你吗？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Good evening, can I help you?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:53.46,0:45:02.01,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你找到需要的…\N{\fnArial\fs30}Have you been able to find anything that…{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:02.10,0:45:05.18,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}很抱歉 我以为…\N{\fnArial\fs30}I'm sorry, I thought I…{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:05.31,0:45:11.44,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}南希 是我啊 亨利\N{\fnArial\fs30}Nancy, it is me, Harry.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:11.56,0:45:15.19,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}别被我吓到\N{\fnArial\fs30}Don't be afraid.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:15.32,0:45:20.74,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我以为你死了30年了\N{\fnArial\fs30}I thought you had been dead these 30 years.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:20.82,0:45:23.32,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我的确死过了…\N{\fnArial\fs30}I have been…{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:23.41,0:45:33.25,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我以为我再也见不到你了\N{\fnArial\fs30}I thought I would never see you again.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:38.84,0:45:42.34,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我们聊了一会\N{\fnArial\fs30}We spoke for a moment or two together.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:42.47,0:45:47.35,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我告诉她一些我的事\N{\fnArial\fs30}I told her some of my story.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:47.43,0:45:48.93,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我不该告诉她\N{\fnArial\fs30}I should have spared telling her{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:49.06,0:45:50.39,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}她的丈夫是个叛徒\N{\fnArial\fs30}that her husband was a traitor{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:50.48,0:45:53.56,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但我冲昏了头 脱口而出\N{\fnArial\fs30}but it all came pouring out of me, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:53.65,0:46:00.40,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}30年入骨的恨啊\N{\fnArial\fs30}30 years of hate.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:00.49,0:46:05.07,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}她被我的话震惊了\N{\fnArial\fs30}She was so effected by what I said, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:05.20,0:46:08.20,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我无法忍受下去\N{\fnArial\fs30}I couldn't stand it.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:08.29,0:46:12.46,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}就逃了出去\N{\fnArial\fs30}I went outside, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:12.58,0:46:15.92,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}之后我看到她走出工作厅\N{\fnArial\fs30}then I saw her come out of the mission{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:16.00,0:46:18.84,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}于是我便跟踪到她家\N{\fnArial\fs30}and I followed her home.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:18.96,0:46:25.64,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我见她走进那所房子 一盏灯亮了\N{\fnArial\fs30}I saw her go into the house, a light came on.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:25.76,0:46:34.15,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我看着她坐在椅子上\N{\fnArial\fs30}I saw her sitting in a chair.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:34.23,0:46:38.44,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}之后他走进那间房间\N{\fnArial\fs30}And then he came into the room.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:40.23,0:46:41.82,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}詹姆斯 我得跟你谈谈\N{\fnArial\fs30}James, I have to talk to you.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:41.94,0:46:43.57,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你干嘛锁门\N{\fnArial\fs30}Why are you locking that door.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:43.66,0:46:44.99,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我说过 别太晚回来\N{\fnArial\fs30}Don't be back late, I said, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:45.11,0:46:46.07,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}别太晚回来 听见没？\N{\fnArial\fs30}don't be back late, didn't I?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:46.20,0:46:47.66,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你外面有男人\N{\fnArial\fs30}You've been with someone.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:47.78,0:46:48.58,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}不…\N{\fnArial\fs30}No…{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:48.66,0:46:49.70,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你背着我找男人\N{\fnArial\fs30}You have been with someone.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:49.83,0:46:51.16,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}没有…\N{\fnArial\fs30}No…{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:51.29,0:46:53.29,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}到底是谁？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Who is it?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:53.41,0:46:58.21,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你毁了我的一生\N{\fnArial\fs30}you've ruined my life.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:58.34,0:47:03.22,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}这么多年 这么多年来\N{\fnArial\fs30}All these years, all these years.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:03.34,0:47:06.30,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}哦 你怎能做出这么…\N{\fnArial\fs30}Oh, how could you do such a thing…{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:06.39,0:47:07.93,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}巴克利夫人 您的茶\N{\fnArial\fs30}Mrs. Barclay, your tea.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:08.01,0:47:09.18,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}这么残忍的事\N{\fnArial\fs30}it was evil.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:09.31,0:47:12.31,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我恨你 我恨你 我恨你 我恨你\N{\fnArial\fs30}I hate you, I hate you, I hate you, I hate you.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:12.43,0:47:14.14,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}不\N{\fnArial\fs30}No…{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:14.27,0:47:16.40,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}看到他抓住她的手\N{\fnArial\fs30}To see him lay a hand on her{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:16.52,0:47:18.31,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我愤怒到了极点\N{\fnArial\fs30}made me mad with anger.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:18.40,0:47:19.82,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我的情感战胜了一切\N{\fnArial\fs30}My feelings overcame me…{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:19.94,0:47:20.98,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}大卫\N{\fnArial\fs30}David…{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:21.11,0:47:21.99,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}您的茶 夫人\N{\fnArial\fs30}Your tea, madam.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:22.07,0:47:23.65,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}大卫 你背叛了他\N{\fnArial\fs30}David, you betrayed him.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:23.78,0:47:25.15,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}这不是真的\N{\fnArial\fs30}It's not true.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:25.28,0:47:28.66,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}但他还活着 我告诉你 我见到他了\N{\fnArial\fs30}But he's alive, I tell you, I've seen him.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:28.74,0:47:31.79,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你说谎 你疯了\N{\fnArial\fs30}You're lying, you're mad.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:44.84,0:47:48.05,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我从未见过一个人有那种表情\N{\fnArial\fs30}He looked as I have never seen a man look.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:48.18,0:47:53.14,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我清楚的感受到他脸上死亡的气息\N{\fnArial\fs30}I read death on his face as plain as anything.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:53.22,0:47:55.73,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我的突然出现像一颗子弹\N{\fnArial\fs30}The bare sight of me was like a bullet{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:55.81,0:48:02.32,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}打穿了他负罪的心\N{\fnArial\fs30}through his guilty heart.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:02.44,0:48:07.24,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}巴克利夫人 巴克利夫人 快开门\N{\fnArial\fs30}Mrs. Barclay, Mrs. Barclay, open the door.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:07.36,0:48:09.78,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他撞上了壁炉架\N{\fnArial\fs30}He smashed onto the fender.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:09.91,0:48:13.70,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}他在倒下去之前就死了\N{\fnArial\fs30}He was dead before he fell.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:30.80,0:48:35.52,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}巴克利夫人 巴克利夫人 快开门\N{\fnArial\fs30}Mrs. Barclay, Mrs. Barclay, open the door.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:45.53,0:48:47.82,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我从南希手中拿走了钥匙\N{\fnArial\fs30}I took the key to the door from Nancy's hand, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:47.95,0:48:49.95,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}本想开门求救\N{\fnArial\fs30}intending to open it and get help.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:50.07,0:48:51.62,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}转念一想我得快点逃走\N{\fnArial\fs30}I thought I'd better get away{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:51.74,0:48:53.70,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}不然就再也洗不清了\N{\fnArial\fs30}or things might look black against me.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:53.83,0:48:56.37,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}匆忙中 我一边把钥匙揣进口袋里\N{\fnArial\fs30}In haste, I thrust the key into my pocket{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:56.45,0:48:57.79,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}一边抓回逃出笼子\N{\fnArial\fs30}whilst I was chasing Teddy, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:57.91,0:49:00.08,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}爬上床帘的泰迪\N{\fnArial\fs30}who'd escaped from his box and run up a curtain.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:00.21,0:49:04.21,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}泰迪\N{\fnArial\fs30}Teddy.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:04.30,0:49:09.34,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}所以 上校是死于\N{\fnArial\fs30}So, the Colonel died before{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:09.47,0:49:12.26,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}撞到壁炉架之前？\N{\fnArial\fs30}he struck his head on the fender?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:12.39,0:49:16.14,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}因为突然的震惊 导致中风猝死\N{\fnArial\fs30}An apoplectic fit, brought on by shock.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:16.27,0:49:19.27,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}伍德先生 假设法医也\N{\fnArial\fs30}Mr. Wood, provided the coroner reaches{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:19.39,0:49:22.06,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}得到相同的结论 那么巴克利夫人\N{\fnArial\fs30}the same conclusion, Mrs. Barclay…{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:22.15,0:49:26.99,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}南希\N{\fnArial\fs30}Nancy.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:27.11,0:49:30.82,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}就会被释放\N{\fnArial\fs30}will be free.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:30.95,0:49:32.45,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我相信您也不会反对把\N{\fnArial\fs30}I trust you would have no objection{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:32.57,0:49:34.45,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}整件事复述给警方吧\N{\fnArial\fs30}to repeating your story to the police, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:34.53,0:49:39.46,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}一旦需要的话？\N{\fnArial\fs30}should the need arise?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:39.58,0:49:45.34,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}福尔摩斯先生 南希现在如何？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Mr. Holmes, how is Nancy?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:45.46,0:49:47.67,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}她人在医院\N{\fnArial\fs30}She's in hospital.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:47.80,0:49:51.43,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}据我所知 她一定会恢复健康\N{\fnArial\fs30}I understand in time she should make a complete recovery.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:51.51,0:49:54.22,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}谢天谢地\N{\fnArial\fs30}Thank God.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:22.50,0:50:25.88,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}嗨 安 真高兴见到你\N{\fnArial\fs30}Hello, Ann, how lovely to see you.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:26.00,0:50:27.25,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你好点了吗？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Are you better?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:27.38,0:50:28.34,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是的 我好多了\N{\fnArial\fs30}Yes, I'm much better.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:34.55,0:50:37.31,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}福尔摩斯 只有一件事我还不明白\N{\fnArial\fs30}Holmes, there's just one thing I don't understand.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:37.39,0:50:40.52,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}如果上校的名字是詹姆斯\N{\fnArial\fs30}If the Colonel's name was James, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:40.60,0:50:43.60,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}而伍德被称呼为亨利或哈利\N{\fnArial\fs30}and Wood was called either Henry or Harry, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:43.73,0:50:46.52,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}那大卫又是谁？\N{\fnArial\fs30}then who the deuce was David?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:46.65,0:50:47.94,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我亲爱的华生\N{\fnArial\fs30}My dear Watson, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:48.07,0:50:50.03,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}大卫这个名字本应告诉我\N{\fnArial\fs30}that name David should have told me{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:50.15,0:50:52.53,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}整个故事 如果我真是你喜欢描述的\N{\fnArial\fs30}the whole story had I been the ideal reasoner, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:52.65,0:50:54.74,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}推理大师的话\N{\fnArial\fs30}which you are so fond of depicting.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:54.86,0:50:57.41,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}可是 唉 我没能推断到\N{\fnArial\fs30}But alas, my powers of deduction failed.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:57.53,0:50:59.62,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你瞧 大卫 在这里\N{\fnArial\fs30}You see, David, in this case, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:59.74,0:51:02.96,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}是一种谴责之辞\N{\fnArial\fs30}was evidently used as a term of reproach.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:03.08,0:51:05.67,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}谴责？\N{\fnArial\fs30}Reproach?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:05.75,0:51:07.54,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你不记得大卫王怎样\N{\fnArial\fs30}Don't you remember how King David{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:07.67,0:51:10.38,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}把赫梯族的乌利亚送到战场\N{\fnArial\fs30}sent Uriah the Hittite into the forefront{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:10.46,0:51:12.55,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}最前线送死 以便有机会\N{\fnArial\fs30}of the battle to die so that he might{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:12.67,0:51:15.18,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}夺取他的女人 拔示巴了吗？\N{\fnArial\fs30}steal his woman, Bathsheba?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:15.26,0:51:17.97,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我想这个故事\N{\fnArial\fs30}I think you will find the story{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:18.10,0:51:21.98,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你会在撒母耳记上篇或下篇中找到\N{\fnArial\fs30}in the first or second book of Samuel.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:22.10,0:51:24.64,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}我对旧约记不太清了\N{\fnArial\fs30}My old testament is a little rusty.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:35.03,0:51:36.82,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}说的不错 福尔摩斯\N{\fnArial\fs30}You're quite right, Holmes, {\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:36.95,0:51:42.12,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}撒母耳记下篇 11：14-17\N{\fnArial\fs30}II Samuel, 11:14-17.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:42.25,0:51:45.67,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你显然已经查过了\N{\fnArial\fs30}You appear to have looked it up yourself{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:45.79,0:51:50.80,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}就在我们从奥尔德肖特回来之后\N{\fnArial\fs30}since we returned home from Aldershot.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:50.92,0:51:55.93,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你是怎么知道的？\N{\fnArial\fs30}How did you know?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:56.05,0:51:58.14,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}你把这张我们在滑铁卢餐厅\N{\fnArial\fs30}You used this bill for our meal{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:58.26,0:52:00.47,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}的账单当作书签 不是吗？\N{\fnArial\fs30}at Waterloo as a bookmarker, did you not?{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:00.60,0:52:03.89,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}漂亮 华生\N{\fnArial\fs30}Excellent, Watson.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:03.98,0:52:10.40,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}雕虫小技 我亲爱的福尔摩斯\N{\fnArial\fs30}Elementary, my dear Holmes.{\r}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:10.48,0:52:15.90,Default,0,0,0,0,,{\blur3}晚安 老伙计\N{\fnArial\fs30}Goodnight, old fellow.{\r}
